<article class="env-proposition" id="EBB0AE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/EBB0AE">Proposition <span data-tag="EBB0AE">6.1.0.1</span>.</a>topos Let $\calC $ be a category. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(A)$"><p>
The category $\calC $ is (equivalent to) the category of sheaves of sets on some Grothendieck site. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(B)$"><p>
The category $\calC $ is (equivalent to) a left-exact localization of the category of presheaves of sets on some small category $\calC _0$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(C)$"><p>
Giraud's axioms!for ordinary topoi Giraud's axioms are satisfied: 
</p>
<ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
The category $\calC $ is presentable (that is, $\calC $ has small colimits and a set of small generators). 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii)$"><p>
Colimits in $\calC $ are universal. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(iii)$"><p>
Coproducts in $\calC $ are disjoint. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(iv)$"><p>
Equivalence relations in $\calC $ are effective. 
</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></p>
